// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'region'. Valid alternatives: ['host', 'port', 'name', 'clusterInstanceHostPattern']
//
// `region:` inside an `Aurora` block. AuroraLexerGrammar declares ONE token set and TWO
// datasource specifications over it, and they take different subsets: `Aurora` takes host,
// port, name and the singular `clusterInstanceHostPattern`; `GlobalAurora` takes host, port,
// name, `region` and the plural `globalClusterInstanceHostPatterns`. `region` and the plural
// form are reachable only through GlobalAurora, and the singular form only through Aurora.
//
// One grammar, two element shapes, an overlapping-but-unequal field set and no naming
// convention separating them -- a rewrite that keys fields on the lexer rather than on the
// chosen specification rule merges the two and accepts a spec that is neither. Both shapes
// are written out in ../fixtures/t2-aurora.pure for the same reason.
//
// `region` is placed first here deliberately: later in the block the parser's error recovery
// drops the alternative list, and the alternative list is the whole value of this fixture.
###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection fixture::neg::AuroraRegion
{
  store: fixture::neg::Db;
  type: Aurora;
  specification: Aurora
  {
    region: 'us-east-1';
    host: 'mydb.cluster-xyz.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com';
    port: 5432;
    name: 'mydb';
  };
  auth: Test;
}
